      When I heard about the tournament (which was the first day it
started), I got convinced by the guys in #nethack to play my games in
it.  It became my unofficial goal to make my first ascension happen
during the tournament, which I completed last night.  Enter teabing the
lawful human female valkyrie.  I picked lawful because of the easy
access to excalibur, which I ended up never getting anyway.

      I started with an extremely friendly early game.  I found an
early touchstone and decided to bless it.  I identified ever gem I came
across, and sold the valuble ones to any shopkeeper who would buy them.
 I used the money to buy protection, got a minetown wish, and before I
knew it, I was in the Mine's End with -16 AC, a truckload of valuble
gems, SDSM, and mojo.  I picked up my luckstone and slowly proceeded
through the dungeon.  I don't normally play as slowly as I did going
from the mines to soko, but I was very afraid to ruin this great start.

      Soko was uneventful.  I got a BoH, which I blessed on site, and
identified "oLS in the zoo.  I stashed away the unIDed or unimportant
wands, scrolls, rings, etc in a dlvl 3 altar stash.  I eventually moved
my stash up to a coaligned altar on dlvl 10.  After a short sac/pray
fest, I got crowned, which was good since I had almost no intrisics at
that point.  I found a "oLS on my way up to Medusa from soko, and
quickly put it on.  I dug down, went upstairs, and let Medusa stone
herself on my armor.  the castle was directly underneath Medusa, so I
headed down there again, but not before taking and blessing Perseus'
boots of levitation.  I actually got close to burning my "oLS after
getting cornered by a bunch of soldiers, but a potion of full healing
helped me out and allowed me to finish them off.  I bagged the wand,
and took it back down to my stash.  it turned out to be at (0:3).  The
wishing commenced.  I had IDed charging shortly before I began wishing,
so I wished up a blessed magic marker for recharging.  I went next with
+3 GoP, +3 HoT, +3 [oMR, +3 speed boots, and 2 blessed scrolls of
genocide.  I used my wrest for another blessed magic marker.  I
commenced a horrendous ritual of getting everything I could out of my
markers, and ended up going back to minetown with -34 AC, mojo encanted
to +6, 3 (remember that) stashed scrolls of gold detection, a spell of
create familiar that I'd forgotten about 2000 turns ago, and a
conspicuous lack of any and all h, L, and ;.  I bought 7 of Izchak's
candles, bagged them, stormed the quest level, and claimed my rightful
orb of weight (which would cause me burdening problem the rest of the
game), and an unthreatening-looking silver bell.

      I decided I was ready for the VotD.  I went to my stash for a
final inventory, and went down.  I also decided to check the storage
rooms in the castle, and found Frost Brand there.  I noticed I hadnt
used the throne in the castle, either, and got a genocide from it.  I
smoked all disenchanters, and raided the VotD.  I got exactly NO wraith
corpses, but kept trudging on.  laying nex to the upstairs in the VotD
was an uncursed geno scroll, which I used to eliminate all rist
monsters.  I found another "oLS on the ground, and bagged it.  I don't
remember much about the demon lords, only that they were unproblematic
enough for me to almost treat them like vrock, since mojo+silver sabre
seemed to smite them before they could teleport away.  I raided Vlad's
tower, and claimed my third "oLS.  Vlad was a pushover, just like I was
told he would be.  I attached the candles to the candelabrum right away
to reduce weight (which was becoming a serious problem).  I went down
to the last level, located the VS, and went back up to try to find the
second fake wizard's tower, which I had missed on my way down.  I went
up, promptly zapped the Wizard with my trusty wand of death, and picked
up the book of the dead.  I gambled a but by #invoking the orb of
weight, which payed off when I got sent to the level right above the
VS.  I performed the invocation, and entered the sanctum.  Rodney payed
me a visit, and I discovered my only WoD was out of charges.  I smaked
him with mojo a few times, and he teleported to temple and stayed there
(an explaination would be appreciated).  I remember that the
priest(esse)s of Moloch game me some trouble, but a /oPoly turned them
into more harmless opponents ("You kill the glass piercer of Moloch!").
 I got hold a cockatrice corpse which was left over, found the door to
the temple (after some difficulty), and stoned the high priest and
Rodneys there (he double troubled himself).  I took the Amulet of
Yendor and went back up (#invoking the orb got me the first few
levels).  I got sent back only 3 times for real (the rest kept me on
the same level).  Rodney visited a few times, but I dont remember how
many.  after escaping Gehennom, I got no visits from Rodney or his
friends.  This would lead me to belive he can't attack you in the main
dungeon, if I didnt notice an instance of "You feel vaguely nervous" on
my stash level.  I grabbed the ?oGD, my wands of digging, and recharged
my wand of death.  I also took a pickaxe, incase I needed it on the
plane of earth (which I did).

      The plane of earth was no real problem.  I located the portal,
and used my wands of digging until they were out.  I ended up using the
pickaxe for the last 4 or so squares between me and the portal cavern.
I dropped the pickaxe and depleted wands of death and headed to the air
plane.  The air elementals gave me no trouble, but would have if I had
decided to fight them instead of running.  When one caught me, I hit it
from inside until it died, which by then had dropped me 20 HP (out of
170).  I was never really worried, though, since I had 3 lifesaves to
fall back on.  The plane of fire was no big deal.  I was fire
resistant, and got to the portal before anything that dealt non-fire
damage got to me.  The water plane was when I realized I had written
one too few scrolls of gold detect.  I did some research, and decided
to weild the amulet to find the portal.  I switched to mojo to kill
some elementals, and never switched back to the amulet.  So there I
was, fumbling around, looking for a message about the location of the
portal that wouldnt come because I was weilding mojo.  This went on for
about 400 turns before I stumbled onto it by chance.  It was astral
time.

      I randomly picked famine to be the first rider to plow through.
I zapped him with my newly charged wand of death, and fought my way
through to the altar, only to find it was neutral.  I flipped a coin,
and it decided to go right, which was death's side.  I hit death twice,
and an angel finished him off with a spell of magic missile that was
meant for me.  I fouht my way through the horde of summoned insects,
and made it to the high altar of Tyr (I could hardly breath at that
point).  I sacrificed the Amulet of Yendor, and looked through my end
of game info.  The only conduct I'd kept was artifact-wishless, but
that's better than nothing.

In any case, this was an awesome experience, and I hope I can do it
with some other roles now :D



